This categorical statement is BS. Just like the goto statement,
carefully targeted save-scumming is a very useful thing.

I used save-scumming for a particular purpose: to learn how to get past
2000' in an effective way.  I saved a character at 2000' so I could
retry it multiple times without wasting time repeating the first 40
levels.  There is a qualitative difference that starts kicking in at dl
40 that you simply cannot learn from repeating the first 40 levels.

Once I became comfortable with play at depth, I stopped scumming.  My
first Angband victory soon followed.

What is a bad habit is promiscuous savescumming, where you are
continuously saving & copying characters simply to avoid death.



